From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: grok-build-providers-verify <verify@invalid>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 16:56:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] Add dynamically controllable raw sampling logs

Record fully shaped raw provider request bodies alongside response SSE chunks. Use one process-wide gate initialized by GROK_LOG_SAMPLING/--log-sampling, keep the tracing layer dynamically interested, and expose hidden /debug sampling on|off|status ACP controls with a full-payload privacy warning.

The JSON fmt formatter walks every ancestor when writing the spans array and panics if any lacks FormattedFields, and sampling events almost always fire under non-sampling agent/shell parent spans. So always forward span lifecycle methods to the inner fmt layer and gate only event emission on target + runtime enable; additionally disable span list / current-span serialization so the formatter never looks up FormattedFields (hard guarantee against the tracing-subscriber panic). A regression test covers both configs.
---
